#. type: Plain text
#: upstream/README:388
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"7. FAQ::\n"
"    Q. \"It doesn't work\"\n"
"    A. There are several reasons why it may be so. One possibility is the\n"
"       following: jhalfs was designed to work against the development "
"versions\n"
"       of the LFS series of books. Consequently changes in a book sometimes\n"
"       break older versions of jhalfs. Before you start pulling out your "
"hair,\n"
"       download the latest version of jhalfs to see if that solves your\n"
"       problem. Note that it may be the other way around. If you want to "
"build\n"
"       an old version of the book, you may have to downgrade your jhalfs\n"
"       version.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: upstream/README:394
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    Q. \"How do I specify the build location?\"\n"
"    A. The original LFS document worked against the well known location\n"
"       /mnt/lfs. This script automates the build of all of the LFS series "
"of\n"
"       books and uses a generic location $BUILDDIR with a default value of\n"
"       /mnt/build_dir. You may change this value to suit your needs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: upstream/README:404
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       The layout below $BUILDDIR is as follows.\n"
"       $BUILDDIR/\n"
"            jhalfs      (Makefile, cmd scripts, logs, etc..)\n"
"            sources     (where packages reside)\n"
"            tools       (temporary cross compiler)\n"
"                ...\n"
"            FHS dir structure\n"
"                ...\n"
"            blfs_root   (files to use blfs-tool if selected to install it)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: upstream/README:413
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    Q. \"What is the function of the SRC_ARCHIVE variable?\"\n"
"    A. When jhalfs runs and packages download was selected, it creates a "
"local\n"
"       copy of the necessary packages in $BUILDDIR/sources by downloading "
"the\n"
"       files. If the variable SRC_ARCHIVE is defined the software will "
"first\n"
"       look in this location for the file and, if found, will copy it to\n"
"       $BUILDDIR/sources.\n"
"       If the files are not found in SRC_ARCHIVE _and_ you have write priv "
"to\n"
"       the directory any downloaded files will be mirrored there.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: upstream/README:416
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    Q. \"How do I set the SRC_ARCHIVE location?\"\n"
"    A. The best way to set the value of SRC_ARCHIVE is\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: upstream/README:418
#, no-wrap
msgid "       export SRC_ARCHIVE=/wherever/you/store/downloaded/packages\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: upstream/README:420
#, no-wrap
msgid "       or you can set the full path in the proper menu entry.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: upstream/README:426
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    Q. \"Why have 2 copies of the files?\"\n"
"    A. The package files must be visible during the chroot phase and this is "
"a\n"
"       simple and reliable method of doing so. This method also handles the\n"
"       boot build method where the final build may be done on a separate\n"
"       machine.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: upstream/README:430
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    Q. \"How could I stop the build at a predefined chosen point?\"\n"
"    A. Launch the Makefile manually passing the last numbered target to be "
"build\n"
"       as the break point. For example:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: upstream/README:432
#, no-wrap
msgid "          make BREAKPOINT=84-bash\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: upstream/README:435
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       The build can be stopped also at the end of a top-level build phase "
"by\n"
"       calling directly the appropriate mk_* target. For example:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: upstream/README:437
#, no-wrap
msgid "          make mk_LUSER\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: upstream/README:439
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       See the Makefile to know the proper target names for that book "
"build.\n"
msgstr ""

